# Propose, Then Finish

## Gate (before code)

For architecture, harness, or product-shape work that is ambiguous or has more than one valid design: ask or plan first. Do not apply until the user confirms.

```text
# ❌ BAD — implement a new orchestration model unasked
# ✅ GOOD — plan or ask; wait; then implement only what was approved
```

Ordinary bugfixes with a named surface and evidence do not need this gate.

## Finish (after approval)

When the user says "Implement the plan", "Build", or "continue": execute remaining approved todos to completion. Do not re-litigate scope, add unasked work, or stop mid-plan.

## Citations

Never cite files, tools, APIs, or line numbers that were not verified on disk in this run. If it was not opened, searched, or executed here, do not claim it exists.
